     1,
     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\" style=\"word-wrap:break-word\">\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Thanks so much, Matt and Daniel. I just tested it and using R 4.0.5 works but the default R v4.1. crashes the session at the plotting stage as you said.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">I am cc’ing the dynr team just so that we know. As far as I am aware, the dynr on CRAN was tested under Rv4.1 and the plotting was fine there. So I think it is just a matter of re-installing the ggplot packages into Rv4.1 on the server.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">I would love to hear more about using Rstudio Cloud. Is it free for now and how can we get started?<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Thanks!<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Sy-Miin<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<div style=\"border:none;border-top:solid #e1e1e1 1.0pt;padding:3.0pt 0in 0in 0in\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b>From:</b> Hansen, Matt &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ma...@psu.edu</a>&gt; <br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b> Saturday, August 28, 2021 12:48 PM<br>\r\n<b>To:</b> Chow, Sy-Miin &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">qu...@psu.edu</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Cc:</b> Kuwahara, Daniel Toshiro &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">dt...@psu.edu</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b> Re: Follow-up: Dynr on RStudio Server Pro<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Hi Sy-Miin,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Thank you for the demo file.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Some good news that the dynr.cook() function should now run successfully.  I believe the resource limits were preventing this from completing. <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">There is currently an issue with ggplot2(), which causes the plotting at the end of the demo to also crash R. Our version of RStudio needs to be updated to properly support R v4.1. Daniel and I will work together to either update RStudio\r\n or change the default R version back to 4.0.5. As a workaround you can use the dropdown in the upper right to switch to R 4.0.5. All the packages in /courses/HDFS538 were built with R 4.1.0 so the typical warning messages will appear but the demo ran successfully\r\n for me. This library can be rebuilt with R 4.0.5 if you prefer, depending on the decision to upgrade RStudio, or you can continue to use the DynamicalSystems library.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">The new version of RStudio Server introduced a lot of new changes so it may be problematic to upgrade since the semester has started but we will try it out.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><a href=\"https://nam10.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fblog.rstudio.com%2F2021%2F06%2F09%2Frstudio-v1-4-update-whats-new%2F&amp;data=04%...%40psu.edu%7C1f6401895d0b4d4befc108d96a4396b9%7C7cf48d453ddb4389a9c1c115526eb52e%7C0%7C0%7C637657660780123189%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C1000&amp;sdata=EsUkEfImZnyPovzC5bJtpCM1BTHiIjOlc5qEea7WJLU%3D&amp;reserved=0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://nam10.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url%3Dhttps%253A%252F%252Fblog.rstudio.com%252F2021%252F06%252F09%252Frstudio-v1-4-update-whats-new%252F%26data%3D04%257C01%257Cquc16%2540psu.edu%257C1f6401895d0b4d4befc108d96a4396b9%257C7cf48d453ddb4389a9c1c115526eb52e%257C0%257C0%257C637657660780123189%257CUnknown%257CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%253D%257C1000%26sdata%3DEsUkEfImZnyPovzC5bJtpCM1BTHiIjOlc5qEea7WJLU%253D%26reserved%3D0&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792521469678000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2UHluv6_8Y-LHqRzvSbkzD\">https://blog.rstudio.com/2021/06/09/rstudio-v1-4-update-whats-new/</a><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">As a side note, I tested dynr on RStudio Cloud (<a href=\"https://nam10.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=http%3A%2F%2Frstudio.cloud%2F&amp;data=04%...%40psu.edu%7C1f6401895d0b4d4befc108d96a4396b9%7C7cf48d453ddb4389a9c1c115526eb52e%7C0%7C0%7C637657660780123189%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C1000&amp;sdata=6n0NpZbA8hZCbSAxaM1iehji1WTIAetA3Dv990AC9h8%3D&amp;reserved=0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://nam10.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url%3Dhttp%253A%252F%252Frstudio.cloud%252F%26data%3D04%257C01%257Cquc16%2540psu.edu%257C1f6401895d0b4d4befc108d96a4396b9%257C7cf48d453ddb4389a9c1c115526eb52e%257C0%257C0%257C637657660780123189%257CUnknown%257CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%253D%257C1000%26sdata%3D6n0NpZbA8hZCbSAxaM1iehji1WTIAetA3Dv990AC9h8%253D%26reserved%3D0&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792521469678000&amp;usg=AOvVaw09qrh1hJdBF8mr5khv1lL6\">http://rstudio.cloud</a>) and\r\n it installed relatively quickly and the demo ran successfully. Using Cloud might be an alternative for you. There’s still no formal university agreement in place for the paid tiers but I know Daniel and his group plans to continue to work on it.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">- Matt<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br>\r\n<br>\r\n<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<blockquote style=\"margin-top:5.0pt;margin-bottom:5.0pt\">\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">On Aug 27, 2021, at 16:44, Chow, Sy-Miin &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">qu...@psu.edu</a>&gt; wrote:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Thanks, Matt and Daniel.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">I am attaching the R file behind the LinearSDE demo. In the line:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">res &lt;- dynr.cook(model, verbose = FALSE)<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">if you change verbose = FALSE to verbose = TRUE, it outputs more intermediate output. See if that is helpful to you guys in anyway.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Thanks!<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Sy-Miin<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div style=\"border:none;border-top:solid #e1e1e1 1.0pt;padding:3.0pt 0in 0in 0in\">\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b>From:</b><span> </span>Hansen, Matt &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ma...@psu.edu</a>&gt;<span> </span><br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b><span> </span>Friday, August 27, 2021 4:38 PM<br>\r\n<b>To:</b><span> </span>Chow, Sy-Miin &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">qu...@psu.edu</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Cc:</b><span> </span>Kuwahara, Daniel Toshiro &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">dt...@psu.edu</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b><span> </span>Re: Follow-up: Dynr on RStudio Server Pro<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Hi Sy-Miin,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">We made some progress testing this. There’s a new course directory at /courses/HDFS538 with a clean install of dynr using R 4.1.0. <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">These are the steps I’m using:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">## Prepend course library to libPaths<br>\r\n.libPaths(c(&quot;/courses/HDFS538/R&quot;, .libPaths()))<br>\r\n<br>\r\n## Load the package<br>\r\nlibrary(dynr)<br>\r\n<br>\r\n## Verify where package was loaded from<br>\r\npath.package(&quot;dynr&quot;)<br>\r\n<br>\r\n## Test &#39;dynr&#39; package functionality<br>\r\ndemo(&#39;LinearSDE&#39;,package=&#39;dynr’)<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Unfortunately, I ran into the same crashing error at the &#39;Starting Hessian calculation’ phase. From the logs I can see that although the UI seems to just stall for a long time it is actually crashing R immediately and the UI is just slow\r\n to respond. I tested it directly within the R console on the server and it ran the demo successfully. I’m working on trying to collect more verbose logs from the coredump that happens in the background. <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Is there a way to run the demo function more verbosely or to output a log from it? It’s possible the issue is within RStudio itself but I have a feeling it is something related to the user environment and possibly DISPLAY settings.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">- Matt<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<blockquote style=\"margin-top:5.0pt;margin-bottom:5.0pt\">\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">On Aug 26, 2021, at 16:02, Hansen, Matt &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ma...@psu.edu</a>&gt; wrote:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Hi Sy-Miin,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">I was able to reproduce the error you described. I tested a few different versions of R 4 with the same result and R 3.6.3 failed with a different error that seemed to be package related. <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">One error I saw in the logs for your account was a command that exceeded the CPU timeout limit, which is 60 seconds. That limit is intended to help with capacity but in my testing R would crash after just 10-20 seconds so I don’t think\r\n that was the issue.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">As you suggested, I think the best option will be to reinstall the latest version from CRAN with R 4.1.0 and Daniel and I can do that.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Couple questions for you:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>               </span><span> </span>Do you want to rename ‘DynamicalSystems’ to ‘HDFS538’ or keep it as is?<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>               </span><span> </span>Can we remove or archive the entire /courses/DynamicalSystems/R package library to try a fresh install in a clean library? Anything else that\r\n would need to be reinstalled or just dynr?<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Thanks,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Matt<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<blockquote style=\"margin-top:5.0pt;margin-bottom:5.0pt\">\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">On Aug 25, 2021, at 13:47, Kuwahara, Daniel Toshiro &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">dt...@psu.edu</a>&gt; wrote:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">I will take a look at it today and get back to you.   Will probably need Matt’s help tomorrow, but we’ll see how it goes.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Daniel.<span> </span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div style=\"border:none;border-top:solid #e1e1e1 1.0pt;padding:3.0pt 0in 0in 0in\">\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b>From:</b><span> </span>Chow, Sy-Miin &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">qu...@psu.edu</a>&gt;<span> </span><br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b><span> </span>Wednesday, August 25, 2021 1:30 PM<br>\r\n<b>To:</b><span> </span>Hansen, Matt &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ma...@psu.edu</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Cc:</b><span> </span>Kuwahara, Daniel Toshiro &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">dt...@psu.edu</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b><span> </span>Re: Follow-up: Dynr on RStudio Server Pro<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt\">Thank you, Matt. Congratuations on your new position. I thought I saw your name on ICDS RISE team the last time I browsed the website.<span> </span></span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;font-family:&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,sans-serif\">😉</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt\"> </span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt\">Daniel, could you please help us trouble shoot? I am hoping to use dynr on the server next Monday.</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt\">I am attaching the instructions for what we typically do after logging in. If dynr is install correctly then demo(‘LinearSDE’,package=’dynr’) should be able to run fully without crashing. If a new version\r\n of R has been installed, then chances are dynr will need to be installed from CRAN again.</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt\">Thanks!</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt\"> </span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt\">s</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt\"> </span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"border:none;border-top:solid #b5c4df 1.0pt;padding:3.0pt 0in 0in 0in\">\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\">From:<span> </span></span></b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\">&quot;Hansen, Matt&quot; &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ma...@psu.edu</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Date:<span> </span></b>Wednesday, August 25, 2021 at 12:29 PM<br>\r\n<b>To:<span> </span></b>&quot;Chow, Sy-Miin&quot; &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">qu...@psu.edu</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Cc:<span> </span></b>&quot;Kuwahara, Daniel Toshiro&quot; &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">dt...@psu.edu</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Subject:<span> </span></b>Re: Follow-up: Dynr on RStudio Server Pro</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Hi Sy-Miin,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Sorry for the delay. I’m traveling this week but wanted to send a quick update. On July 1st I moved into a new role with ICDS. Daniel Kuwahara (Cc’d) will be supporting RStudio and other data science services for courses.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Yes, dynr should still be installed in your DynamicalSystems course directory. And if you’d like, that can be renamed for your course.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Hopefully Daniel can help troubleshoot the error and crashing. I don’t have access to a computer but I’ll try to take a look also when I get back.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">The only thing that comes to mind is that new versions of R were installed and the default version may have changed since you last used it. You may want to check to see which version dynr was built with. Maybe update or reinstall it if\r\n there have been any significant changes. You should have full access to make changes to the DynamicalSystems library.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Hope that helps. I should be able to take a look at this tomorrow morning and help Daniel troubleshoot.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">- Matt<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:12.0pt\"><br>\r\nOn Aug 24, 2021, at 23:52, Chow, Sy-Miin &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">qu...@psu.edu</a>&gt; wrote:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<blockquote style=\"margin-top:5.0pt;margin-bottom:5.0pt\">\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt\">Hi Matt:</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt\">Just want to follow-up to give you more information.</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt\"> </span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt\">I was able to load and run demo(‘LinearSDE’,package=’dynr’) fine after doing</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:13.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:black;background:#f2f2f2\">libPaths(c(&quot;/courses/DynamicalSystems/R&quot;, .libPaths()))”4.   Navigate to the “Files” panel and click on the “...” button in the top right corner.\r\n Set Path to Folder to /courses/DynamicalSystems. You should see some folders containing demo scripts for this workshop.</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt\"> </span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt\">But after optimization is called and when it is doing Hessian calculation, it took forever and then crashed every single time. Insights are greatly appreciated!</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt\"> </span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt\">Thanks!</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt\">Sy-Miin</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt\"> </span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"border:none;border-top:solid #b5c4df 1.0pt;padding:3.0pt 0in 0in 0in\">\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\">From:<span> </span></span></b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\">&quot;Chow, Sy-Miin&quot; &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">qu...@psu.edu</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Date:<span> </span></b>Tuesday, August 24, 2021 at 12:53 PM<br>\r\n<b>To:<span> </span></b>&quot;Hansen, Matt&quot; &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ma...@psu.edu</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Subject:<span> </span></b>Dynr on RStudio Server Pro</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Hi Matt,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">I am hoping to teach with the R package, dynr, this semester in my class (HDFS538). However, when I tried to login, even though I do see all my previous folders there, doesn&#39;t seem like dynr is installed. My own attempt to do install.packages\r\n directly from the classroom computer didn&#39;t work out (or took eternity). <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Could you please kindly help us install dynr again so my whole class can use it while logged in with their own access IDs? Thanks so much!<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Sincerely,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Sy-Miin<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">On May 13, 2021 10:03 AM, &quot;Hansen, Matt&quot; &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ma...@psu.edu</a>&gt; wrote:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border:none;border-left:solid #cccccc 1.0pt;padding:0in 0in 0in 6.0pt;margin-left:4.8pt;margin-top:5.0pt;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:5.0pt\">\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">You’re very welcome and glad it worked out. And thank you for mentioning your fall class. We’re still trying to develop more scalable cloud options for teaching with R/Python and so this feedback is very valuable.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">-<span> </span><span style=\"color:black;background:yellow\">Matt</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<blockquote style=\"margin-top:5.0pt;margin-bottom:5.0pt\">\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">On May 12, 2021, at 16:49, Chow, Sy-Miin &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">qu...@psu.edu</a>&gt; wrote:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Just want to thank you again for the timely help!!!! I hope to continue to use dynr on the server in my class in Fall 2021. Thanks!<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Sy-Miin<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"border:none;border-top:solid #b5c4df 1.0pt;padding:3.0pt 0in 0in 0in\">\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\">From: </span></b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\">&quot;<span style=\"color:black;background:yellow\">Hansen</span>,<span> </span><span style=\"color:black;background:yellow\">Matt</span>&quot;\r\n &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ma...@psu.edu</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Date: </b>Wednesday, May 12, 2021 at 1:27 P<br>\r\n<b>To: </b>&quot;Chow, Sy-Miin&quot; &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">qu...@psu.edu</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Subject: </b>Re: Proble</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">I was able to re-install dynr into &quot;/courses/DynamicalSystems/R&quot; and everything seems to be working now.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">-<span> </span><span style=\"color:black;background:yellow\">Matt</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:12.0pt\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<blockquote style=\"margin-top:5.0pt;margin-bottom:5.0pt\">\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">On May 12, 2021, at 13:05,<span> </span><span style=\"color:black;background:yellow\">Hansen</span>,<span> </span><span style=\"color:black;background:yellow\">Matt</span><span> </span>&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\"><span style=\"color:purple\">ma...@psu.edu</span></a>&gt;\r\n wrote:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">It looks like the other packages in the custom library are installed and working and have the correct permissions. Installing dynr should be all that is needed. Just may take some time. <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">-<span> </span><span style=\"color:black;background:yellow\">Matt</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:12.0pt\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<blockquote style=\"margin-top:5.0pt;margin-bottom:5.0pt\">\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">On May 12, 2021, at 12:49,<span> </span><span style=\"color:black;background:yellow\">Hansen</span>,<span> </span><span style=\"color:black;background:yellow\">Matt</span><span> </span>&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\"><span style=\"color:purple\">ma...@psu.edu</span></a>&gt;\r\n wrote:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Oh no! So it looks like the R library still exists and there are some packages in it but you are correct that dynr seems to be missing from it. With the regular install.packages command, that might be installing into your local home library.\r\n I used the the ‘lib’ option to specify the custom library:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">install.packages(&quot;dynr&quot;, lib = &quot;/courses/DynamicalSystems/R”).<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Did you want to try running that command or would you like me to? I just want to avoid installing to the same library at the same time.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">If you run into a CPU timeout during the installation, you may just have to run it again and let it pickup where it left off.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">-<span> </span><span style=\"color:black;background:yellow\">Matt</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:12.0pt\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<blockquote style=\"margin-top:5.0pt;margin-bottom:5.0pt\">\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">On May 12, 2021, at 12:23, Chow, Sy-Miin &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\"><span style=\"color:purple\">qu...@psu.edu</span></a>&gt; wrote:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Hi<span> </span><span style=\"color:black;background:yellow\">Matt</span>:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">I accidentally overwrote the “courses/DynamicalSystems/R” folder, which presumably contained the dynr and other R packages. I tried to now do “install.packages(‘dynr’) but it seems to be building a whole lot of R packages from source, not\r\n just R. Help~!!!! Did I accidentally break the server?<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">The workshop is starting at 1:30pm and I am not quite sure what to do.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Hope you somehow see this in time. Thanks in advance!<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">s<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"border:none;border-top:solid #b5c4df 1.0pt;padding:3.0pt 0in 0in 0in\">\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\">From: </span></b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\">&quot;<span style=\"color:black;background:yellow\">Hansen</span>,<span> </span><span style=\"color:black;background:yellow\">Matt</span>&quot;\r\n &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\"><span style=\"color:purple\">ma...@psu.edu</span></a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Date: </b>Tuesday, May 11, 2021 at 11:16 A<br>\r\n<b>To: </b>&quot;Chow, Sy-Miin&quot; &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\"><span style=\"color:purple\">qu...@psu.edu</span></a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Subject: </b>Re: dynr on Rstudio Connect server</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Hi Sy-Miin,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">That’s great to hear the new server is working well for you. <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Unfortunately, new server doesn’t have a direct PASS connection. We’re still exploring doing this and we need to meet with the PASS team to get a roadmap on their service but no progress yet. The reason we opted to not use PASS is due instability\r\n for home directories, permission issues and scalability concerns on the previous server.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">The easiest option for participants would be to use the Files pane, select the files and click More &gt; Explort function to download a zip file. Or they could also use sftp/scp to move files to PASS or push them to Git.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Here is a link you could share with them - <a href=\"https://nam10.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fsupport.rstudio.com%2Fhc%2Fen-us%2Farticles%2F200713893-Uploading-and-Downloading-Files&amp;data=04%...%40psu.edu%7C1f6401895d0b4d4befc108d96a4396b9%7C7cf48d453ddb4389a9c1c115526eb52e%7C0%7C0%7C637657660780133190%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C1000&amp;sdata=8LYTN2p5FyI03Tv1AszUvtrvXBEJyINVz%2FsVezekGkI%3D&amp;reserved=0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://nam10.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url%3Dhttps%253A%252F%252Fsupport.rstudio.com%252Fhc%252Fen-us%252Farticles%252F200713893-Uploading-and-Downloading-Files%26data%3D04%257C01%257Cquc16%2540psu.edu%257C1f6401895d0b4d4befc108d96a4396b9%257C7cf48d453ddb4389a9c1c115526eb52e%257C0%257C0%257C637657660780133190%257CUnknown%257CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%253D%257C1000%26sdata%3D8LYTN2p5FyI03Tv1AszUvtrvXBEJyINVz%252FsVezekGkI%253D%26reserved%3D0&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792521469680000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1J1LJLzyYwC9n9yn6j84YL\"><span style=\"color:purple\">https://support.rstudio.com/hc/en-us/articles/200713893-Uploading-and-Downloading-Files</span></a><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">I’m not exactly sure why you might be seeing inconsistencies when connecting to PASS but it’s possible there are some replication delays or maybe a difference between U-Drive and PASS.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">-<span> </span><span style=\"color:black;background:yellow\">Matt</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:12.0pt\"><br>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<blockquote style=\"margin-top:5.0pt;margin-bottom:5.0pt\">\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">On May 11, 2021, at 08:54, Chow, Sy-Miin &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\"><span style=\"color:purple\">qu...@psu.edu</span></a>&gt; wrote:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Thank you,<span> </span><span style=\"color:black;background:yellow\">Matt</span>. I logged in to the new RStudio Server Pro and everything seems to work. I was able to run dynr, upload files to courses/DynamicalSystems\r\n etc. Thanks!<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">However, I do have a question. How do participants save a copy of their files on their local computer. The strange thing is, I tried saving a file to HOME. I thought this would be my PASS drive or something of that sort. But when I tried\r\n to log in to my PASS drive via<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><a href=\"https://webfiles.psu.edu/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://webfiles.psu.edu/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792521469680000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3bL5V8m5gJUvpwMMK2--hS\"><span style=\"color:purple\">https://webfiles.psu.edu</span></a> or <a href=\"https://explorer.pass.psu.edu/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://explorer.pass.psu.edu/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792521469680000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0UUZyS0bymuuoAiaIZFHzD\"><span style=\"color:purple\">https://explorer.pass.psu.edu/</span></a><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">I don’t see the new file that was just saved. I do see the other files that are on the PASS drive BEFORE I save that one new file. It is like the file is being saved in a parallel universe. Any insights?<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">In fact, the same thing seems to be happening when I was trying to upload files to my own website at <a href=\"http://personal.psu.edu/quc16\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://personal.psu.edu/quc16&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792521469680000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0QNkK7_LxrIo2NkThDfcJI\"><span style=\"color:purple\">personal.psu.edu/quc16</span></a>. T